  "notes": "Rove 0.1.13 beta for macOS arm64.\n\n- Improve responsiveness of large Request sidebars, Script call target lists and Performance target selectors while retaining complete search and keyboard selection.\n- Reduce repeated Script catalog and open-tab metadata work during editing. Show Save feedback before preparing the captured workspace write.\n- Store larger local editor recovery in transactional IndexedDB, migrate previous recovery copies, and wait for recovery hydration before opening the workbench.\n- Add fixed one-time Support tiers with cocoa artwork and explicit Stripe sandbox links. Sandbox payments are tests only and charge no real money.\n\nThis Mac-first release raises the signed minimum supported version to 0.1.13. Supported older Mac clients must update at their next launch after receiving the verified policy. Windows packages are not included; existing Windows assets and the legacy Windows manifest remain unchanged.\n\nBuilt locally from source f85ee6f813d97f74dface0da5b7bd310cde534b1 without GitHub Actions. The Mac app uses ad-hoc platform signing and is not Apple-notarized; production updater signatures authenticate the archive and policy separately. Installed upgrade/restart and personal-data preservation acceptance have not been performed.\n",
